.TH CWE-98 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-98 \- Improper Control of Filename for Include/Require Statement in PHP Program ('PHP Remote File Inclusion')
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The PHP application receives input from an upstream component, but it does not restrict or incorrectly restricts the input before its usage in require, include, or similar functions. In certain versions and configurations of PHP, this can allow an attacker to specify a URL to a remote location from which the product will obtain the code to execute. In other cases in association with path traversal, the attacker can specify a local file that may contain executable statements that can be parsed by PHP.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB2\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2025\-68645
Synacor Zimbra Collaboration Suite (ZCS), added 2026\-01\-22.
.PP
Synacor Zimbra Collaboration Suite (ZCS) PHP Remote File Inclusion Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Synacor Zimbra Collaboration Suite (ZCS) contains a PHP remote file inclusion vulnerability that could allow for remote attackers to craft requests to the /h/rest endpoint to influence internal request dispatching, allowing inclusion of arbitrary files from the WebRoot directory.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, or discontinue use.
 Due 2026\-02\-12.
.PP
